    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p class="updated">
        <strong>Last updated: September 2026</strong>
    </p>

    <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how information is handled when you use
        <strong>Rock Simulator</strong>, a mobile game developed by
        <strong>RhythymGames</strong>.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Information Collection</h2>

    <p>
        RhythymGames does not directly collect or store personal information
        such as your name, address, phone number, or email address through
        Rock Simulator.
    </p>

    <p>
        However, the game may use third-party services that automatically
        collect certain information required to provide advertising,
        application functionality, security, diagnostics, and performance
        services.
    </p>

    <p>This information may include, depending on the services used:</p>

    <ul>
        <li>Device model and device information</li>
        <li>Operating system and version</li>
        <li>Advertising identifiers</li>
        <li>IP address or approximate network information</li>
        <li>Application usage information</li>
        <li>Crash and diagnostic information</li>
        <li>Information required to display advertisements</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. Third-Party Services</h2>

    <p>
        Rock Simulator may use third-party services to provide advertising,
        application distribution, and other functionality.
    </p>

    <p>These services may include:</p>

    <ul>
        <li>Unity Ads</li>
        <li>Google Play Services</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        Third-party service providers may collect and process information
        according to their own privacy policies. RhythymGames does not
        control the information practices of these third-party services.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Advertising</h2>

    <p>
        Rock Simulator may display advertisements provided by third-party
        advertising services.
    </p>

    <p>
        Advertising providers may automatically process information such as
        device information, advertising identifiers, application information,
        and other technical information to provide, measure, and improve
        advertisements.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Internet Connection</h2>

    <p>
        Rock Simulator requires an internet connection to access certain
        game functionality and services, including online services and
        advertisements.
    </p>

    <p>
        Network-related information may be processed by the operating system,
        Google Play services, advertising providers, or other third-party
        services used by the application.
    </p>

    <h2>5. How Information May Be Used</h2>

    <p>
        Information processed by third-party services may be used for purposes
        including:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Providing advertisements</li>
        <li>Measuring advertising performance</li>
        <li>Improving application stability</li>
        <li>Diagnosing technical problems</li>
        <li>Preventing fraud and abuse</li>
        <li>Providing and maintaining application functionality</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Children's Privacy</h2>

    <p>
        Rock Simulator is intended for a general audience. We do not
        intentionally request or collect personal information directly from
        children.
    </p>

    <p>
        Third-party services integrated into the application may have their
        own policies and age-related requirements. Parents and guardians
        should review the privacy policies of those services where
        appropriate.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Data Security</h2>

    <p>
        We take reasonable measures to protect information handled through
        the application. However, no method of electronic transmission or
        storage can be guaranteed to be completely secure.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>

    <p>
        RhythymGames does not directly maintain a database of personal user
        information collected through Rock Simulator.
    </p>

    <p>
        Information collected by third-party services is subject to the
        respective service provider's retention and deletion policies.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Third-Party Privacy Policies</h2>

    <p>
        Third-party services used by Rock Simulator may have their own
        privacy policies explaining how they collect, use, retain, and share
        information.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>

    <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will
        be posted on this page with an updated "Last updated" date.
    </p>

